{
  "id": "andon-barred",
  "description": "The kōshi face: no middle rail, three bars standing the whole height of the opening at quarter spacing. Every bar is a stile in its own right, lapped into the top and bottom rails, so the panel gains eight joints and no new kind of joint. The light is striped rather than gridded, which is the difference between a lamp you read by and a lamp you look at.",
